    "details": "<p><strong>About The Event:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Think you&rsquo;re the best coder in your college? Prove it against the best from other colleges, win cash prizes, and get a certificate, all for free.</li>\n<li>Code in Java or Python on 21st November 2026 at CEM Kolaghat.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Prizes And Rewards:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><strong>1st: ₹5,000</strong></li>\n<li><strong>2nd: ₹3,000</strong></li>\n<li><strong>3rd: ₹2,000</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Certificates</strong> for participants</li>\n<li><strong>Free lunch</strong> for every participant</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Details:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><strong>Date: Saturday, 21st November 2026</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Reporting Time: 10:30 AM</strong></li>\n<li>Commencement: 11:00 AM</li>\n<li>Venue: College of Engineering &amp; Management, Kolaghat (offline, on campus)</li>\n<li>Languages: Java / Python</li>\n<li><strong>Registration Fee: FREE</strong></li>\n<li>Last Date to Register: 15th November 2026, 11:59 PM</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Open to students from all colleges. (only UG)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Competition Format:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Individual participation only (no teams)</li>\n<li>Depending on the number of participants, the contest may have more than one round.</li>\n<li>Every participant is provided a computer inside the contest hall.</li>\n<li>Winners (1st, 2nd, 3rd) will be announced at the valedictory session on the same day.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules And Regulations:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Participation is individual only.</li>\n<li>No travelling allowance (TA) will be reimbursed.</li>\n<li>Every contestant must carry their latest college ID card. Participation will be rejected without it.</li>\n<li>A computer will be provided to every participant inside the contest hall.</li>\n<li>No electronic gadgets (laptop, mobile phone, smart watch, pendrive, memory card) are allowed inside the contest hall.</li>\n<li>Late arrivals will not be allowed, so report by 10:30 AM.</li>\n<li><strong>E-certificates will be emailed to all participants a few days after the contest.</strong></li>\n<li>Prize money will be given by cheque along with a printed certificate of merit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Contact Details:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Mr. Subhrangsu Das (TAC Advisor &amp; Mentor): +91 7908957796</li>\n<li>Email: <a href=\"mailto:subhrangsudas31@gmail.com\">subhrangsudas31@gmail.com</a> (9 AM &ndash; 9 PM)</li>\n<li>Instagram: @tac_cemkolaghat</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Register now and code your way to victory!</p>",
